2 Semantic indexing and search layer
A raw file system alone does not let AI “find all in the drive.” You need an indexing layer that understands file contents. Modern AI architectures use vector databases to store embeddings of documents, images or audio. This allows semantic search rather than simple keyword matching. Key points from a comparative analysis of leading vector databases
